# CostOps

Internal multi-provider FinOps. Spec: `docs/Neetrino_CostOps_CURSOR_SPEC.md`. Stack: `docs/TECH_CARD.md`.

- **Size B.** Feature layout: `src/features`, `src/core`, `src/providers`, `src/shared`. Not a monorepo. Not NestJS.
- Do **not** modify `neetrino/neon`. It stays live until 7-day parity is proven.
- Provider I/O lives only in `src/providers/<key>/`. Core cost, budget, sync orchestration, and alerts stay provider-agnostic.
- Primary budget object is **Project × Provider**. Do not assume identical daily spend across projects.
- Never treat missing or stale cost as `$0`. Every aggregate exposes freshness (`fresh` / `partial` / `final` / `stale` / `error` / `missing`).
- Pull model: CostOps owns alerts. Evaluate after a successful current-day sync. Dedupe per `budgetRuleId` + UTC day. Escalate from `lastNotifiedCostUsd`.
- Do not add Grafana, Apprise, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Kubernetes, or extra notification platforms in v1.
- Reuse proven Neon dashboard UX: period filters, charts, cards/list, inline limits, retry, Telegram, escalation, SyncRun.
- UI must be clearly more refined than the live Neon dashboard ([`docs/DESIGN.md`](../../docs/DESIGN.md)). **No gradients.** No leftover template. Verify in the browser.
- `OLD_NEON_PROJECT_DATABASE_URL` is read-only history from `neetrino/neon`. Never use it as CostOps `DATABASE_URL`. See `docs/OLD_NEON_DATABASE.md`.
- Validate provider API responses with Zod at the adapter boundary. No `any` on those boundaries.
- Schema changes go through `safe-database-migration`. Update `docs/PROGRESS.md` after milestones.
- `docs/TECH_CARD.md` is confirmed. Follow `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`. Do not retire old Neon until parity tests pass.
- Neon env names match the baseline app: `NEON_API_KEY`, `NEON_ORG_ID`. Do not add `NEON_PRIMARY_*` aliases.
- Every provider adapter must expose a create-token URL and auth-failure detection. Warn 30d / 7d / expired and on 401. See `docs/CREDENTIAL_ROTATION.md`.
